ion  and the City of London itself so London  is kind of the center of the world at  that time it's one of the biggest cities  in the world it's the center of the  Industrial Revolution and one of the  things that we're doing differently this  year is that it the players are not  unravelling a strange mystery the game  the setup is laid out before them at the  start of the game the Templars are  firmly in control of London  you know the Templar Grandmaster is and  our two assassins decide by themselves  to go and destroy the hold that the  Templars have on the city so it makes  for a nice open playground an open  setting for our players to engage in so  it reminds me a little bit of the Borgia  influence in was it Brotherhood when you  know you know you know who the bad guys  are already and you go take them down  yeah one of the ways that you can do  that in syndicate is gang walls yeah  basically can you tell me a little bit  about this because we saw a little bit  in the gameplay trailer so one of the  things the ways that Jacob and Evie will  try to take back London is true the  street gangs so the Templars control the  street gang and through those gangs they  control the working-classes  so one of the ways Jacob and Evie will  fight back against the Templar is create  by creating their own gang and then from  borough to borough conquered the city  and expand the influence of their gang  and they're gonna be a super important  tool for the player in the game in the  sense that you'll be able to recruit and  power them up and they'll follow you  around so if you recruit for example  five five gang members and you up on a  vehicle because you can climb on any  vehicle that you want they'll hop on the  vehicle would you open the doors get in  but if there's not enough space they'll  hijack a vehicle of their own so you're  moving through the city with your own  gang so it feels really cool fresh and  different than what we've seen in the  past so you mentioned briefly vehicles  there and they have we're getting a very  big GTA vibe from that you know you just  go hijack it run some people over the  question I have so in Assassin's Creed  typically you can't kill civilians  you'll get desynchronized if you kill  civilian  what if say I'm trembling down the  street in a carriage that I've stolen  and I accidentally knock into someone  who's on the way to the bakery or  something you'll see that our civilians  are very good at dodging those cards so  they jump out of the way because I don't  think it would be fun for the players to  just be synchronized as they mow true -  true civilians so still we keep that  part of the franchise but we've done a  lot of efforts to make sure those  civilians move out of the way for the  player to have fun that is good to hear  no absolutely so the vehicles knew you  you're kind of reinventing the South a  little bit as well so we're very used to  this cover based hiding in the hay bales  what but you also bring back whistling  which is a great thing that I really  missed so he took me a little bit about  how you're reinventing the game that is  so well known for hiding in the shadows  so last year Assassin's Creed unity and  introduced a feature that was much  awaited by our fans the crouch so and  you could snap on on the corners of  buildings so what we're trying to do  differently this year is we keep trying  to improve the game so we're moving to a  soft snap instead of having a hard snap  so it's much more accessible and fluid  fluidity is really a key word for us  this year making the experience feel  more fluid for players but also giving  for me stealth is about manipulating the  environment so players have more tools  now than ever we're bringing back the  whistle but also we're trying to think  about our different tools can improve  stealth showing knives are a good  example so instead of just being used to  kill enemies you can throw them on the  wall and create a distraction so st